{"report":"## Your audience\nCore buyers index highest in the 25-to-34 bracket (peaking at 25 to 29), with solid over-indexing down to age 24 and younger. Older demographics (35 and up) show a strong negative affinity. Gender indexing skews slightly male, fitting classic West Coast skate and street culture lines.\n\n## Artists & music they love\n- **Isaiah Rashad**: High 97% match; hits the smooth, introspective West Coast hip-hop wave core to your sound.\n- **Chester Watson**: 94% alignment; brings underground, atmospheric rap flows favored by your demographic.\n- **Joey Fatts**: 93% match; connects directly to street-level Cali hustle and hard-edged production.\n- **Kembe X**: 93% affinity; bridges alternative hip-hop and raw underground energy.\n- **Yung Simmie**: 92% match; appeals to loyal followers of gritty underground tape culture.\n- **Chuuwee**: 92% alignment; reinforces regional West Coast pride and consistent independent grind.\n\n## Brands they also wear\n- **Stüssy**: 88% match; the ultimate blueprint for heritage skate and streetwear credibility.\n- **A Bathing Ape**: 87% affinity; speaks to an appetite for bold graphic identities and iconic logos.\n- **Anti Social Social Club**: 87% match; taps into high-impact text logos and mood-driven drops.\n- **Undefeated**: 87% alignment; aligns with sports-heritage graphics and street-culture curation.\n- **Champion**: 86% match; provides the trusted heavyweight fleece foundation for oversized hoodies.\n\n## Where to pop up\n- **Los Angeles, CA**: Dense concentration across metro hotspots; ideal for a pop-up leveraging heavy West Coast skate and hip-hop roots.\n- **San Francisco, CA**: Strong Bay Area affinity spanning San Francisco and Oakland; perfect for tapping into local skate subcultures.\n- **Portland, OR**: High concentration in the Pacific Northwest; great audience fit for outdoor-leaning streetwear and nylon tracksuits.\n- **New York, NY**: Major urban cluster in Brooklyn/Manhattan; prime market for 